    "created_at": "2025-07-15T10:06:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-07-15T10:06:57Z",
    "body": "> The empty string is a perfectly good keyword\n\nThe thing is it's never actually the canonical keyword. As far as I'm aware it's currently always mapped to a different keyword. So in that sense it's much closer to a special state.\n\nMy gut is that Empty is both non-legacy and used enough (I count at least 9 usages) that it deserves some special treatment.\n\nThe other cases where multiple keywords map to the same state I think can probably be left to spec prose. Without some very funky WebIDL grammar we wouldn't be able that mapping behaviour in the IDL anyway.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
