    "updated_at": "2025-07-15T11:00:27Z",
    "body": "I don't think there are many actually. I just went through them again and I find `shape` (from `area`) and `autocapitalize` (global). What else is there? And for those two it seems reasonable to just handle them as distinct states that are treated the same. But the empty string is very common and it would definitely be much nicer if it was normalized away early on.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
