    "body": ">  just went through them again and I find shape (from area) and autocapitalize (global).\n\nShape isn't specified to be limited to only known values so can just use \"[Reflect]\" the keyword and state design is purely in spec handling of those states rather than related to reflection.\n\nAutocapitalize isn't specced to use reflection it has a custom getter that handles its weirdness. (Though it could use a ReflectSetter if we added one).\n\nSo neither of these actually need any special casing in IDL because they just don't use reflection currently. I think we should prioritise codifying the existing usages of reflection rather than trying to account for edge cases like this.\n\nThough if we can handle simple getters with a [ReflectGetter] and simple setters with a [ReflectSetter] then that would be beneficial regardless.",
